  "source": "[P \\.or./ Q]\nStates:\nwhen: P, Q is \\\\statement\nthat:\n. anyOf:\n  . P\n  . Q\nDocumented:\n. called: \"$P?$ or $Q?$\"\n. written: \"P? \\lor Q?\"\n. description: \"The disjunction of $P$ and $Q$. The statement $P \\text{ or } Q$\n                holds when at least one of $P$ and $Q$ holds. As is standard in\n                mathematics, the *or* is inclusive: it also holds when both do.\"\nId: \"f401f869-7009-411a-bc01-9a76ffa07901\"",
